# Files the PUBLIC scaffold owns. `bin/export-to-public.sh` syncs the private tree over this clone
# with `rsync --delete` and KEEPS exactly these paths — everything else is replaced by the export.
# Every entry must exist here: a keep entry naming nothing is an exclusion in disguise (P7).
# One list, in the repo it protects, so a reader of either side sees the same set.
LICENSE
LICENSE.GPL-3.0
README.md
RELEASE.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md
.gitignore
.editorconfig
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github/
.claude/
bin/hooks/
instances/
backend/pyproject.toml
.export-keep
.public-last-export
